The magnitude of a complex number of the form $a+bi$ is given by $\sqrt{a^2+b^2}$. Applying this to the given complex number $\frac12 - \frac38i$, we have:

\begin{align*}
\left|\frac12 - \frac38i\right| &= \sqrt{\left(\frac12\right)^2 + \left(-\frac38\right)^2} \\
&= \sqrt{\frac14 + \frac{9}{64}} \\
&= \sqrt{\frac{16}{64} + \frac{9}{64}} \\
&= \sqrt{\frac{25}{64}} \\
&= \frac{5}{8}
\end{align*}

So, $\left|\frac12 - \frac38i\right| = \boxed{\frac58}$.The answer is: \frac{5}{8}

