&= 2x^2 + 14x - 5x - 35 \\
&= 2x^2 + 9x - 35.
\end{align*}

Next, we expand $(x + 5)(2x - 1)$:
\begin{align*}
(x + 5)(2x - 1) &= x \cdot 2x + x \cdot (-1) + 5 \cdot 2x + 5 \cdot (-1) \\
&= 2x^2 - x + 10x - 5 \\
&= 2x^2 + 9x - 5.
\end{align*}

Now we subtract the second expression from the first:
\begin{align*}
(2x^2 + 9x - 35) - (2x^2 + 9x - 5) &= 2x^2 + 9x - 35 - 2x^2 - 9x + 5 \\
&= 2x^2 - 2x^2 + 9x - 9x - 35 + 5 \\
&= 0 + 0 - 30 \\
&= \boxed{-30}.
